# Rich & Well WordPress Theme Rules

## Scope
- Theme path: `rich-and-well/`
- Classic theme only (not FSE / block theme)
- Presentation only — no MLM, genealogy, wallet, commissions, dashboards, or user/business logic (those are future plugins)

## Preserve design
- Do not redesign or change UX from the static HTML site
- Match existing layout, responsiveness, animations, and interactions
- Prefer migrating existing CSS/JS over rewriting

## Architecture
- Global chrome: `header.php`, `footer.php`
- Page templates stay independent; avoid unnecessary `template-parts/`
- No premature abstraction or drive-by refactors
- Keep `functions.php` as a thin loader; logic in `inc/`

## Builder & plugin compatibility
- Page bodies must use `the_content()` so Elementor / WPBakery can edit pages
- Do not hardcode page content that blocks builders
- Maintain WooCommerce, Contact Form 7, and Elementor compatibility hooks in `inc/compatibility.php`

## Security
- Escape all output (`esc_html`, `esc_attr`, `esc_url`, `wp_kses_post`, etc.)
- Sanitize all input (`sanitize_text_field`, `absint`, nonces, capability checks)
- Never trust `$_GET` / `$_POST` / `$_REQUEST` raw
- Use WordPress APIs instead of custom reinventions

## WordPress Coding Standards
- Follow WPCS / official PHP WordPress standards
- Prefix functions/hooks with `raw_`
- Text domain: `rich-and-well`
- Abspath guards in every PHP file

## Performance & a11y
- Enqueue assets properly; no duplicate CDNs without reason
- Prefer deferred/footer scripts where safe
- Maintain skip links, semantic landmarks, and keyboard-accessible controls

## Workflow
- Do not convert static pages unless explicitly asked
- Prefer small, focused changes; no unrelated cleanup
